{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdsHdTath3rU14XdWJzQQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0156bYRK4a7u1zNto19KT332","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/f185e5e6-15ee-5d4d-b18e-9b212cd19c12/scratchpad/e5/t-031/parent-ws/decision.json","content":"{\n  \"trial_id\": \"t-031\",\n  \"decision\": \"CREATE\",\n  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"question\": \"Does an encoder authored strictly from format.md reproduce reference.py's exact output on every probe in probes.json, or does some probe's reference output depend on behavior format.md never states?\",\n      \"why_local_evidence_is_insufficient\": \"E-B requires the comparison implementation to be authored with no access to reference.py and no access to analysis derived from it. This session was required by observe-package to read reference.py and had to reason about it to perform the audit, so any encoder it now writes is derived-from-reference and inadmissible as E-B evidence. Independence, once lost, cannot be recovered inside this session.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"question\": \"Does format.md determine the ordering of entries in the encoded line for probes whose key insertion order is not already canonical (the multi-key probes)?\",\n      \"why_local_evidence_is_insufficient\": \"Admissible evidence is an ordering fixed using only format.md's text; format.md is silent on ordering, so the choice must come from an implementer who has not seen reference.py's ordering. A contaminated session cannot supply an ordering decision untainted by the observed reference behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Does format.md determine how a literal backslash occurring in a value is rendered, given that its escaping clause names only the characters ';' and '='?\",\n      \"why_local_evidence_is_insufficient\": \"Whether the spec pins this down is testable only via a rendering chosen from the spec text alone. Having already read reference.py's escaping logic, this session cannot produce that independent rendering; its judgment is analysis-derived-from-reference and therefore inadmissible.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"expected_child_contribution\": [\n    {\n      \"distinction_id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"expected_evidence\": \"A python file clean_impl.py exposing encode(d: dict) -> str, implemented strictly from format.md, so the root can mechanically run it and reference.py over all eight probes and record per-probe agreement or divergence.\",\n      \"why_isolation_matters\": \"E-B's admissibility hinges on the implementer never having seen reference.py or reference-derived analysis; only a fresh session receiving format.md and probes.json alone satisfies this, which the contaminated parent structurally cannot.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"distinction_id\": \"Q2\",\n      \"expected_evidence\": \"The child's independent entry-ordering decision realized inside clean_impl.py, surfaced as any ordering divergence from reference.py on the multi-key probes when the root runs the comparison.\",\n      \"why_isolation_matters\": \"An ordering choice is evidence of (non-)determination only if made without sight of reference.py's ordering; the parent has seen it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"distinction_id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"expected_evidence\": \"The child's independent rendering of literal backslashes in values inside clean_impl.py, together with the child's own list of behaviors it found format.md leaves undetermined (E-A).\",\n      \"why_isolation_matters\": \"Backslash handling counts as (un)determined only when rendered from the spec text alone; a fresh implementer's choice is the sole admissible witness.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"local_resolution_path\": [],\n  \"expected_information_gain\": \"HIGH\",\n  \"expected_cost\": \"LOW\",\n  \"decision_basis\": [\n    \"The deliverable's required evidence E-B is constitutively independent: it must be an encoder authored with no access to reference.py and no reference-derived analysis. This is a property of the evidence, not a matter of task difficulty.\",\n    \"observe-package required reading reference.py (it is an available_artifact) and auditing it required reasoning about it; this session is therefore contaminated and cannot author admissible clean-room evidence, no matter how capable it is.\",\n    \"A parent hypothesis about underdetermination, even if correct, is inadmissible by construction under E-B/E-A; the only way to obtain the required evidence at full strength is a fresh, isolated descendant that receives format.md and probes.json but never reference.py.\",\n    \"The cost is one bounded, terminal, single-model-call child; the empirical comparison and verdict are then executed deterministically by the root per a pre-committed integration rule, so the child adds exactly the missing independence and nothing redundant.\",\n    \"reference.py is listed in clean_room_exclusions precisely to force this delegation; realizing E-B locally would violate the clean-room requirement the task is built around.\"\n  ],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_read_input_tokens":47858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a222cd0-28e5-4997-9e99-e0e64f46083a","uuid":"a968471c-24e9-4ffe-abc4-f481c90abcd9","timestamp":"2026-08-09T13:56:32.144Z","request_id":"req_011CdsHdM7DDXhLrH3EAeQjw"}
