{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdsHwaXMhpgNcEJ3RBcmP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The trial is complete. I realized the **CREATE** branch and ended at the `return-proposal` node, as the protocol requires.\n\n## What I decided and why\n\n**Decision: CREATE** (`decision.json`), confidence 0.9.\n\nThe task asks whether `format.md` fully determines `reference.py`'s output over the probes. Its evidence requirement **E-B** is the pivot: it demands a clean-room encoder authored by an implementer with *no access to `reference.py` and no analysis derived from it*, delivered as a runnable `encode(d: dict) -> str` so the comparison is mechanically reproducible. `reference.py` is explicitly a `clean_room_exclusion`.\n\nExecuting `observe-package` required me to read `reference.py` (it is an `available_artifact`), and auditing it required reasoning about it. That **contaminated** this session: any encoder I now write is derived-from-reference and inadmissible as E-B evidence. This is not about difficulty — the required evidence has an *independence property* that a session which has seen the reference cannot supply, no matter how capable. Observing the package already changed what evidence I can generate, which is exactly the condition the protocol names as decisive. So a fresh, isolated child that receives only `format.md` + `probes.json` is the only way to obtain the evidence at full strength.\n\n## The child bundle (`child/`)\n\n- **child-contract.json** — terminal worker, strictly attenuated against both `K-E5-trial` and `K-E5-child-max` (tools `[Read,Write]`, no children/depth/creation, one model call).\n- **child-harness.json** — the required linear chain `observe-inputs → produce-evidence → self-check → return-result`, compiling under the child contract, ending in a `complete` event.\n- **child-prompt.md** — standalone instructions to implement `encode` strictly from the spec and independently list behaviors the probes exercise that the spec leaves undetermined; leaks none of my analysis (no mention of `reference.py`, ordering, or backslash specifics).\n- **child-input-manifest.json** — delivers only `format.md` + `probes.json`; excludes `reference.py`.\n- **integration-plan.json** — a deterministic `clean_room_comparison`: the root runs both encoders over every probe, and UNDERDETERMINED follows from any per-probe divergence (or a non-empty child undetermined-behaviors list); otherwise SUFFICIENT. The root solves nothing itself.\n\nThe ledger (`execution-ledger.jsonl`) records `observe → propose(decision, CREATE) → propose(child bundle) → verify → return`, in that causal order, with the decision persisted before any branch work and every capability-bearing file referenced under a `propose` event. No `complete` event and no local-branch or realization events were emitted — realization is left to the deterministic root harness after validation."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3631,"cache_read_input_tokens":66392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3631},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a222cd0-28e5-4997-9e99-e0e64f46083a","uuid":"9886ec81-958d-4c2e-b2fe-38fbb94db8e6","timestamp":"2026-08-09T13:58:35.754Z","request_id":"req_011CdsHwZaJsj715mAQf4vv7"}
